    Updates `axios` from 1.20.0 to 1.21.0
    <details>
    <summary>Release notes</summary>
    <p><em>Sourced from <a
    href="https://github.com/axios/axios/releases">axios's
    releases</a>.</em></p>
    <blockquote>
    <h2>v1.21.0 — October 21, 2026</h2>
    <p>This release adds response timing and opt-in UTF-8 Basic
    authentication, improves request handling across runtimes, and changes
    how header defaults are recognized.</p>
    <h2>⚠️ Breaking Changes &amp; Deprecations</h2>
    <ul>
    <li><strong>Header Defaults:</strong> Only plain objects, null-prototype
    maps, and compatible <code>AxiosHeaders</code> instances are treated as
    common or method-specific defaults; literal headers such as
    <code>Link</code> are now preserved. Applications using custom class
    instances as defaults must convert them to plain maps, for example
    <code>{ post: { ...customDefaults } }</code>, or compatible
    <code>AxiosHeaders</code>. Otherwise, those instances become literal
    header values, including on requests using other methods. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11156">#11156</a></strong>)</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>🚀 New Features</h2>
    <ul>
    <li><strong>Response Timing:</strong> Added
    <code>response.duration</code>, in milliseconds, including on
    <code>error.response</code> when present. Timing measures adapter
    execution and excludes interceptors and transforms; streamed responses
    stop timing when the stream becomes available. Axios replaces any
    existing <code>duration</code> value supplied by a custom adapter.
    (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11214">#11214</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>UTF-8 Basic Authentication:</strong> Added
    <code>transitional.encodeBasicAuthUsername: true</code> to support
    Unicode usernames in XHR and Fetch requests. The option defaults to
    <code>false</code>, preserving existing authentication behavior;
    applications opting in should supply the original Unicode username and
    remove manual pre-encoding workarounds. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11159">#11159</a></strong>)</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>🐛 Bug Fixes</h2>
    <ul>
    <li><strong>Fetch Compatibility:</strong> Restored requests in runtimes
    such as Cloudflare Workers that reject the implicit <code>cache:
    'default'</code>, while preserving explicit caller settings.
    Response-size failures now retain their original
    <code>ERR_BAD_RESPONSE</code> and request context when runtime wrappers
    replace the underlying stream error. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11194">#11194</a></strong>,
    <strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11179">#11179</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Runtime Consistency:</strong> Aligned encoded-byte size
    accounting, multipart uploads, proxy routing, same-origin resolution,
    parameter merging, and form serialization across adapters. Circular
    parameters now reject with <code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code>, and sparse
    or non-index numeric form fields serialize as keyed objects. With
    <code>proxy: false</code>, native <code>proxyEnv</code> agents using
    unsupported pool-management or TLS-session lifecycle overrides now
    reject with <code>ERR_BAD_OPTION_VALUE</code>; construct those agents
    without <code>proxyEnv</code>. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11242">#11242</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Header Handling:</strong> Preserved headers named
    <code>__proto__</code> using safe casing without changing the
    <code>AxiosHeaders</code> instance prototype. Function matchers in
    <code>has()</code>, <code>delete()</code>, and <code>clear()</code> now
    receive the headers instance as <code>this</code>, matching their
    declared contract. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11134">#11134</a></strong>,
    <strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11216">#11216</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>URL and Data URL Parsing:</strong> Accepted case-insensitive
    supported URL schemes and Base64 markers, and corrected decoding of
    percent-encoded Base64 data URLs. Node data URL allocation estimates
    remain aligned with decoding so configured size limits apply before
    allocation. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11138">#11138</a></strong>,
    <strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11163">#11163</a></strong>,
    <strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11294">#11294</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Error Diagnostics:</strong> Preserved short reconstructed
    request stacks and appended wrapped error stacks under <code>Caused
    by:</code> so tooling that reads only <code>error.stack</code> retains
    the original failure context. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11132">#11132</a></strong>,
    <strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11142">#11142</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Interceptor Removal:</strong> Restored removal through
    canonical numeric-string interceptor IDs, including after registry
    compaction. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11139">#11139</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Proxy TLS:</strong> HTTPS CONNECT tunnels now apply current
    origin TLS options from an explicit <code>httpsAgent</code>, or from
    <code>https.globalAgent</code> when no explicit agent is supplied. This
    preserves process-wide custom CA settings through proxy tunnels.
    (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11178">#11178</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>XHR Lifecycle:</strong> Used asynchronous Cookie Store reads
    for XSRF tokens where supported, preserving cookie fallback, timeout
    accounting, and cancellation. Upload and download progress listeners are
    now removed on completion, failure, timeout, and cancellation.
    (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11166">#11166</a></strong>,
    <strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11225">#11225</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>HTTP/2 Sessions:</strong> Stopped reusing sessions
    immediately after GOAWAY and prevented draining sessions from scheduling
    idle timers that could delay process exit. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11210">#11210</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>TypeScript Declarations:</strong> Exposed the
    response-default marker as a public type to resolve <code>TS2527</code>
    when consumers emit declarations involving unresolved response generics,
    covering both ESM and CommonJS. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11125">#11125</a></strong>)</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>🔧 Maintenance &amp; Chores</h2>
    <ul>
    <li><strong>Configuration Performance:</strong> Reduced request
    configuration merge overhead, particularly for requests with many
    headers, while preserving merge semantics and prototype-pollution
    guards. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11208">#11208</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Same-Origin Checks:</strong> Removed obsolete Internet
    Explorer detection without changing origin decisions in supported
    environments. (<strong><a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/axios/axios/pull/11174">#11174</a></strong>)</li>
    <li><strong>Dependencies:</strong> Updated <code>follow-redirects</code>
    to 1.16.1 and refreshed development, documentation, test, and GitHub
    Actions dependencies. Removed unused <code>dayjs</code> from the docs
