    Updates `i18next-browser-languagedetector` from 8.2.1 to 8.3.0
    <details>
    <summary>Changelog</summary>
    <p><em>Sourced from <a
    href="https://github.com/i18next/i18next-browser-languageDetector/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md">i18next-browser-languagedetector's
    changelog</a>.</em></p>
    <blockquote>
    <h3>8.3.0</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>security: a detected language must now have the shape i18next 26.7
    accepts for a language code from outside (its
    <code>isSafeLanguageCode</code>): letters, digits, <code>-</code>,
    <code>_</code>, <code>@</code> and <code>.</code> (no <code>..</code>),
    at most 128 characters. It replaces the list of XSS patterns, which
    missed values like <code>&lt;b&gt;x&lt;/b&gt;</code> or <code>&quot;
    onmouseover=&quot;x()</code> from the query string, a cookie or storage,
    which then became the language; apps put it into <code>&lt;html
    lang=&quot;...&quot;&gt;</code>. Compatibility note: a value with other
    characters (spaces, slashes, quotes) is now skipped and the next
    detector is used; codes like <code>en_US</code>, <code>zh_Hant_TW</code>
    or <code>sr@latin</code> still pass, and i18next 27 refuses such codes
    from outside as well.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>8.2.4</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>fix: <code>lookupFromSubdomainIndex</code> counts hostname labels
    again, so with <code>1</code>, <code>dev.en.example.com</code> is
    detected as <code>en</code>. Since 6.1.5 the index picked a regex group
    instead, and any index other than <code>0</code> returned a part of the
    domain (<code>en.exampl</code>, <code>example.com</code>). Index
    <code>0</code> (the default) works as before. Thanks <a
    href="https://github.com/lprnmns"><code>@​lprnmns</code></a> <a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/i18next/i18next-browser-languageDetector/pull/329">329</a></li>
    </ul>
    <h3>8.2.3</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>fix: the subdomain detector now detects language tags with script
    and region subtags, so <code>pt-BR.site.com</code>,
    <code>zh-Hans-CN.site.com</code>, <code>es-419.site.com</code> and
    <code>sr-Latn.site.com</code> are detected as <code>pt-BR</code>,
    <code>zh-Hans-CN</code>, <code>es-419</code> and <code>sr-Latn</code>.
    The pattern only accepted 2 to 5 word characters, without hyphens. Other
