    Updates `@playwright/test` from 1.64.0 to 1.65.0
    <details>
    <summary>Release notes</summary>
    <p><em>Sourced from <a
    href="https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/releases">@​playwright/test's
    releases</a>.</em></p>
    <blockquote>
    <h2>v1.65.0</h2>
    <h2>🥟 Run tests with Bun</h2>
    <p>The test runner now runs under <a href="https://bun.com">Bun</a>. Bun
    transpiles your TypeScript test files itself, so Playwright does not use
    Babel or its compilation cache. Pass the <code>--bun</code> flag,
    because without it <code>bunx playwright test</code> runs on
    Node.js:</p>
    <pre lang="bash"><code>bunx --bun playwright test
    </code></pre>
    <p>Our CI runs the test runner tests under Bun 1.4.3 on Linux. Some
    features work differently under Bun:</p>
    <ul>
    <li>There is no watch mode. UI mode does not run tests again when files
    change, and <code>--only-changed</code> does not follow imports.</li>
    <li>Bun loads modules itself, so <code>--tsconfig</code> and the JSX
    options in <code>tsconfig.json</code> have no effect, and custom ESM
    loaders are not supported.</li>
    <li>Stack traces do not include async frames, and API names do not
    include the class name: <code>click</code> instead of
    <code>locator.click</code>. This changes some step locations, step
    titles and error messages.</li>
    <li>Console output of a test does not get into the trace and UI
    mode.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>🚨 Reports with only failures</h2>
    <p>New <a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/test-reporters#failures-reporter"><code>failures</code></a>
    reporter prints failures and successful retries as they occur, followed
    by a summary, without progress output.</p>
    <p>New <code>onlyFailures</code> option of the HTML, JSON and JUnit
    reporters <a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/test-reporters#report-only-failures">keeps
    only</a> tests with unexpected outcomes, flaky tests and interrupted
    tests:</p>
    <pre lang="js"><code>// playwright.config.ts
    import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';
    <p>export default defineConfig({
    reporter: [
    ['failures'],
    ['html', { onlyFailures: true }],
    ],
    });
    </code></pre></p>
    <h2>🎯 Test runner</h2>
    <ul>
    <li>
    <p>New built-in <code>-exclusive-</code> <a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/test-parallel#test-locks">test
    lock</a> runs a test only when no other tests are running. All other
    tests continue to run in parallel with each other:</p>
    <pre lang="js"><code>test('restart the server', { lock: '-exclusive-' },
    async () =&gt; {
      // No other test runs while this one is running.
    });
    </code></pre>
    </li>
    <li>
    <p><a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-test#test-skip">test.skip()</a>,
    <a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-test#test-fixme">test.fixme()</a>,
    <a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-test#test-fail">test.fail()</a>
    and <a
    href="https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-test#test-slow">test.slow()</a>
    now accept only a description. It is recorded in the test
    annotation:</p>
    <pre lang="js"><code>test('upload a file', async ({ page }) =&gt; {
      test.skip('Not implemented yet');
    });
    </code></pre>
    </li>
    </ul>
    <!-- raw HTML omitted -->
